1
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:10,860
One breezy morning, Pooh laid out a picnic:
a cloth, a pot of honey,

2
00:00:10,910 --> 00:00:14,070
and a space just the size of a Piglet.

3
00:00:14,610 --> 00:00:17,060
“For me?” asked Piglet.

4
00:00:17,110 --> 00:00:19,400
“For us,” said Pooh.

5
00:00:19,950 --> 00:00:23,470
But the wind, it seemed,
wanted to come too.

6
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:30,170
So off they went, over the heather
and under the pines,

7
00:00:30,220 --> 00:00:33,620
with the bees close behind,
just in case.

8
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:39,300
“Perhaps,” said Pooh,
“it knows somewhere nicer.”

9
00:00:43,230 --> 00:00:44,700
It did.

10
00:00:47,760 --> 00:00:51,150
It wasn’t quite the picnic Pooh had planned.

11
00:00:51,780 --> 00:00:57,600
But with Piglet beside him,
it was a perfectly wonderful afternoon.

